{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And if the household be too little for a lamb.</b> And if they are too few to constitute one lamb — that they cannot eat it and it would come to leftover. <b>Then shall he and his neighbor take, etc.</b> This is its meaning according to its plain sense. And there is further midrash in it: to teach that after they have been counted for it, they may diminish and withdraw from it and be counted for another lamb; but if they came to withdraw and diminish — <b>from being a lamb</b> — they may diminish while the lamb still stands, while it is alive and not from after it has been slaughtered (Pesaḥim 9)." "<b>According to the counting.</b> A reckoning, as in ״מִכְסַת הָעֶרְכְּךָ״ (Leviticus 27)." "<b>According to his eating.</b> What is fit for eating — excluding the sick person and the elder who cannot eat an olive's bulk (Mekhilta)." "<b>You shall count.</b> ״תִּתְמְנוּן״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:33.399223994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}